# DESCRIPTION

Section 6 describes the formats of files, and the conventions they keep.

There is one text format, ndb(6): records of `key=value` tuples, one record to a line with indented lines continuing it.
Configuration, manifests, the namespace files, the manual's index and most of what servers print are ndb, and one strict parser reads them all, so no program formats or parses it by hand.

A format's page lists its keys; a key it does not know is an error, not ignored.
The manual's own pages are in guide(6); text is UTF-8 (utf(6)).

